Physical Location Registry

Copyright 2026 Summon Software Labs.

Physical Location Registry is an open-source, vendor-neutral runtime for stable
physical addressing of sites, rooms, rows, racks, rack units, cages and zones in
a data center, with explicit move, rename and replacement semantics.

This product is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See the
LICENSE file in this distribution for the full license text.

Physical Location Registry does not collect or transmit any telemetry. Every
record it writes is written to local files chosen by the operator and never
leaves the machine running the software.

Physical Location Registry accepts contributions from individuals and
organizations on the terms of the Apache License 2.0 without requiring a
Contributor License Agreement (CLA). See CONTRIBUTING.md for contribution
guidance.
